==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fo|non|ríkr}}, from {{inh|fo|gem-pro|*rīkijaz}}, a derivative of {{m|gem-pro|*rīks||king, ruler}}, itself a borrowing from {{der|fo|cel-pro|*rīxs}}, from {{der|fo|ine-pro|*h₃rḗǵs}}, from {{der|fo|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|fo|/ˈɹʊiːkʊɹ/}}
*: {{rhymes|fo|ʊiːkʊɹ|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{fo-adj|ríkari|ríkastur}}

# [[rich]]

====Declension====
{{fo-decl-adj-1|rík}}

==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|ríkr}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*rīkijaz}}, a derivative of {{m|gem-pro|*rīks||king, ruler}}, itself a borrowing from {{der|is|cel-pro|*rīxs}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*h₃rḗǵs}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈriːkʏr/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|iːkʏr|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|@@}}

# [[rich]], [[wealthy]]
#: {{ux|is|Mamma mín er '''rík'''.|My mom is '''rich'''.}}
# [[powerful]], [[strong]], [[compelling]]
#: {{uxi|is|Ég hef '''ríkar''' ástæður.|I have '''compelling''' reasons.}}

